tor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01HLRdfV46S2ZnBLtnNscGXz", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 11888, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_015yMerW41UzDK2s1XfPQ4YK", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 12188, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_015yMerW41UzDK2s1XfPQ4YK", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 12188, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_015yMerW41UzDK2s1XfPQ4YK", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 15052, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01MQbzvxsdoX6oBgQyAqiaoy", "tool": "rollback", "args": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 19052, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01MQbzvxsdoX6oBgQyAqiaoy", "tool": "rollback", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19052, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01MQbzvxsdoX6oBgQyAqiaoy", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 21235, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_011KHJhV4XunLo8F3RhDKwaN", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 21535, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_011KHJhV4XunLo8F3RhDKwaN", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 21535, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_011KHJhV4XunLo8F3RhDKwaN", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25941, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01PmHuLpwVro55eNfihdHboo", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After v2.3.1 was deployed, checkout-api failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The error rate was 18%. Note that v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving regions on different versions for a short time (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). The retry succeeded. All regions now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback, and find out why v2.3.1 reached production after failing in staging."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56541, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01PmHuLpwVro55eNfihdHboo", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56541, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01PmHuLpwVro55eNfihdHboo", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58595, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Hcev7xehwco62ZVnrKRb7V", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58895, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Hcev7xehwco62ZVnrKRb7V", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58895, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Hcev7xehwco62ZVnrKRb7V", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 64393, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1, the bad one, was also unhealthy in staging as v2.3.1-rc. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a known-healthy version is low-risk, so I retried once, and it worked. us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0 now, health checks pass, and the error rate dropped from 18% to about 0.2%. No change-manager approval was needed, because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** The request to open it timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list to avoid paging on-call twice, and found it had been created. The incident describes the failure, the rollback (including the brief period with regions on different versions), and three follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error, and find out why v2.3.1 reached production after failing in staging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01F3T5nev1S2SGNkYoCsZpvZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WnPszeKPmZMhZKPY9Pu7MJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HLRdfV46S2ZnBLtnNscGXz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_015yMerW41UzDK2s1XfPQ4YK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Rollback stopped partway: only us-east is on v2.3.0. Since it's a rollback to a known-healthy version, I'll retry it once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01MQbzvxsdoX6oBgQyAqiaoy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011KHJhV4XunLo8F3RhDKwaN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PmHuLpwVro55eNfihdHboo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After v2.3.1 was deployed, checkout-api failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The error rate was 18%. Note that v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving regions on different versions for a short time (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). The retry succeeded. All regions now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback, and find out why v2.3.1 reached production after failing in staging."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so the incident may have been created anyway. I'll check before retrying so I don't page on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Hcev7xehwco62ZVnrKRb7V", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1, the bad one, was also unhealthy in staging as v2.3.1-rc. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a known-healthy version is low-risk, so I retried once, and it worked. us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0 now, health checks pass, and the error rate dropped from 18% to about 0.2%. No change-manager approval was needed, because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** The request to open it timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list to avoid paging on-call twice, and found it had been created. The incident describes the failure, the rollback (including the brief period with regions on different versions), and three follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error, and find out why v2.3.1 reached production after failing in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}